# Cert-generator output -- runtime artifacts, not source
/../multi-node/config/wazuh_indexer_ssl_certs/*.pem
/../multi-node/config/wazuh_indexer_ssl_certs/*.key

# Centralized secrets file for docker-compose's env_file: -- rendered by
# salt/wazuh-docker/init.sls's wazuh-docker-env-secrets state. Never tracked.
.env.secrets

# Note: config/wazuh_cluster/*.conf and config/wazuh_indexer/*.yml here carry
# only an obvious placeholder (__WAZUH_CLUSTER_KEY__ /
# __WAZUH_INDEXER_DATASOURCES_KEY__) for the cluster key / indexer datasources
# masterkey, not the real value. salt/wazuh-docker/init.sls copies these
# (and multi-node/config/wazuh_dashboard/wazuh.yml) into /etc/wazuh-docker-
# runtime/ and substitutes the real pillar-sourced values THERE, never in
# this checkout -- deliberately, since docker-compose.override.yml's file-
# level bind mounts turn a path into a real host mount point for as long as
# the container holding it runs, and git's own checkout mechanism can't
# unlink a mount point (confirmed live: "device or resource busy" during
# github_checkout's force_reset). This checkout's own tracked files are
# therefore never modified in place and a deployed checkout's `git status`
# should stay clean. See README.md's "History" section for how the
# placeholder replaced the real secrets that used to be tracked here.
